avid-reader contains a partial Rust port of pyavb
(https://github.com/markreidvfx/pyavb, commit ff64e06b60077ecabe5db3fef239898b08363898):
the AVB container/object-table layout and the read() logic of the classes listed in
src/objects.rs. pyavb is MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2022 Mark Reid; its license text is in
LICENSE-pyavb. The MXF header reader (src/mxf.rs) is written from SMPTE ST 377-1 and does not
derive from pyavb or Filmcraft.

src/interpolation.rs ports all numerical functions in pyavb's
src/avb/interpolation.py at the same pinned revision (MIT, Copyright (c) 2022
Mark Reid). A synthetic oracle fixture was generated from that revision.
Matching pyavb calculations does not establish Avid rendering equivalence.

src/parameter_registry_data.rs contains the 735 UUID/name entries from pyavb's
src/avb/parameter_uuids.py at the same pinned revision (MIT, Copyright (c) 2022
Mark Reid). The names were extracted from AAF files by pyavb and are not
independently verified Avid UI meanings.

src/bin_nav.rs ports the read-only Bin navigation helpers from pyavb's
src/avb/bin.py at the same pinned revision (MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Mark Reid).

src/bin_writer.rs ports bounded payload serialization for ABIN, BINF, ASET,
BVst and ATTR from pyavb bin.py and attributes.py at the same pinned revision
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2022 Mark Reid). It does not write complete AVB files.

src/misc_writer.rs ports bounded payload serialization for APOS, ABOB, DIDP,
MCBR, MCMR and TMBC from pyavb misc.py at the same pinned revision (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2022 Mark Reid). It does not write complete AVB files.

src/animatte.rs is a port of FilmCraft's bounded AniMatte reader
(https://github.com/storytold/filmcraft, PR #1056 at dd9457a978040899dfb171e63d9979c41678ad5c,
crates/interchange/src/avid_bin/animatte.rs), MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and
the FilmCraft contributors; its license text is in LICENSE-filmcraft. Ported at the User's
request (2026-10-20); this crate does not depend on or link FilmCraft code.
